{"abstract":"This is a conversation between Gopinaath Kannabiran and Anna Brynskov who both work in Sexuality and HCI. They discuss intersections between theoretical outsets from critical disability, cyberfeminism and ecofeminism. Brynskov’s prototype is presented side by side with a vision for future design research in disability spheres and in regards to materials for breathing together.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kannabiran, Gopinaath","Brynskov, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798525"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pratt Institute"],"keyword":["Cyberfeminism","Ecofeminism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex disability and hci","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217237236","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798525","identifier":[{"id":"85217237236","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e299c0a-d3e0-48f1-a332-034868a0ec54"],"keyword":["Critical Disability","Cyberfeminism","Design Research in Disability","Ecofeminism","Sexuality and HCI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CBE1DE9C48AAE6DECEC2F7237666411"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"pratt institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pratt Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gopinaath","key":"kannabiranpau","last":"Kannabiran","name":"Kannabiran, Gopinaath","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"brynskovpau","last":"Brynskov","locid":"b611f406-3531-4b9a-a511-831d28cf62ef","name":"Brynskov, Anna","orcid":"0009-0009-7029-6728","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3706590","issn":["10725520","15583449"],"issn_org":["10725520"],"issue":"1","journal":"interactions","pages":"14-15","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"interactions","title_org":"ACM Interactions","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217237236"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e299c0a-d3e0-48f1-a332-034868a0ec54"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sex, Disability and HCI","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798525","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The IoT European Large-Scale Pilots Programme includes the innovation consortia that are collaborating to foster the deployment of IoT solutions in Europe through the integration of advanced IoT technologies across the value chain, demonstration of multiple IoT applications at scale and in a usage context, and as close as possible to operational conditions. The programme projects are targeted, goal-driven initiatives that propose IoT approaches to specific real-life industrial/societal challenges. They are autonomous entities that involve stakeholders from the supply side to the demand side, and contain all the technological and innovation elements, the tasks related to the use, application and deployment as well as the development, testing and integration activities. This chapter describes the IoT Large Scale Pilot Programme initiative together with all involved actors. These actors include the coordination and support actions CREATE-IoT and U4IoT, being them drivers of the programme, and all five IoT Large-Scale Pilot projects, namely ACTIVAGE, IoF2020, MONICA, SynchroniCity and AUTOPILOT.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Brynskov, Martin","Guillén, Sergio","Sala, Pilar","Fico, Guiseppe","Arredondo, María Teresa","Cano, Alicia","Posada, Jorge","Gutiérrez, Germán","Palau, Carlos","Votis, Konstantinos","Verdouw, Cor","Wolfert, Sjaak","Beers, George","Sundmaeker, Harald","Chatzikostas, Grigoris","Ziegler, Sébastien","Hemmens, Christopher","Holst, Marita","Ståhlbröst, Anna","Scudiero, Lucio","Reale, Cesco","Krco, Srdjan","Drajic, Dejan","Eisenhauer, Markus","Jahn, Marco","Valiño, Javier","Gluhak, Alexander","Vermesan, Ovidiu","Fischer, François","Lenz, Olivier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-269213"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","F