{"abstract":"Escherichia coli (E. coli) may be implicated in the pathogenesis of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), as implied from a higher prevalence of mucosa-associated E. coli in the gut of IBD-affected individuals. However, it is unclear whether different non-diarrheagenic E. coli spp. segregate from each other in their ability to promote intestinal inflammation. Herein we compared the inflammation-inducing properties of non-diarrheagenic LF82, 691-04A, E. coli Nissle 1917 (ECN) and eleven new intestinal isolates from different locations in five IBD patients and one healthy control. Viable E. coli were cultured with human monocyte-derived dendritic cells (moDCs) and monolayers of intestinal epithelial cells (IECs), followed by analysis of secreted cytokines, intracellular levels of reactive oxygen species and cellular death. The IBD-associated E. coli LF82 induced the same dose-dependent inflammatory cytokine profile as ECN and ten of the new E. coli isolates displayed as high level IL-12p70, IL-1β, IL-23 and TNF-α from moDCs irrespective of their site of isolation (ileum/colon/faeces), disease origin (diseased/non-diseased) or known virulence factors. Contrarily, 691-04A and one new IBD E. coli isolate induced a different cellular phenotype with enhanced killing of moDCs and IECs, coupled to elevated IL-18. The cytopathic nature of 691-04A and one other IBD E. coli isolate suggests that colonization with specific non-diarrheagenic E. coli could promote intestinal barrier leakage and profound intestinal inflammation, while LF82, ECN and the remaining non-diarrheagenic E. coli isolates hold notorious pro-inflammatory characteristics that can progress inflammation in case of intestinal barrier leakage.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Stina Rikke","Mirsepasi-Lauridsen, Hengameh Chloé","Thysen, Anna Hammerich","Brynskov, Jørn","Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki","Petersen, Andreas Munk","Pedersen, Anders Elm","Brix, Susanne"],"cuid":["S02-098.91-034222"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cell Death","Cytokine profile","Dendritic cells","Inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distinct inflammatory and cytopathic characteristics of i escherichia coli i isolates from inflammatory bowel disease patients","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128102244/Distinct_inflammatory_and_cytopathic_characteristics.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.91-034222","identifier":[{"id":"84989820515","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26522075","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-48b91c1d-4eb9-4897-b109-bc37446d09cf","ku-ecbc4551-18e7-47bf-8117-e344a1a2e618"],"keyword":["Cell death","Cytokine profile","Dendritic cells","IBD-associated E. coli","Inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7BA7934423FBD97BF9520BCC234FE38D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128102244/Distinct_inflammatory_and_cytopathic_characteristics.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Rikke","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7535381e-e2f3-475a-991e-be73b60b38a0","name":"Jensen, Stina Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hengameh Chloé","key":"mirsepasilauridsenpau","last":"Mirsepasi-Lauridsen","name":"Mirsepasi-Lauridsen, Hengameh Chloé","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Hammerich","key":"thysenpau","last":"Thysen","locid":"e6276c87-6ec3-4627-9e10-51580ff87bf0","name":"Thysen, Anna Hammerich","orcid":"0000-0002-2914-1099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørn","key":"brynskovpau","last":"Brynskov","name":"Brynskov, Jørn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Angeliki","key":"krogfeltpau","last":"Krogfelt","name":"Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Andreas Munk","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"a6630d5c-ef4a-4a85-906f-ca5bdfa35414","name":"Petersen, Andreas Munk","orcid":"0000-0003-0531-0553","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders Elm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dcd1cfb9-0ba1-4151-897d-f04233bd6c91","name":"Pedersen, Anders Elm","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"brixpau","last":"Brix","name":"Brix, Susanne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26522075"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijmm.2015.10.002","issn":["14384221","16180607"],"issn_org":["14384221"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Journal of Medical Microbiology","pages":"925-936","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Medical Microbiology","volume":"305"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84989820515"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-48b91c1d-4eb9-4897-b109-bc37446d09cf","ku-ecbc4551-18e7-47bf-8117-e344a1a2e618"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Distinct inflammatory and cytopathic characteristics of <i>Escherichia coli</i> isolates from inflammatory bowel disease patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.91-034222","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"During the first decade of the 2000s, the newspaper industry in Denmark came under severe pressure from a number of technical and social innovations. Those include the spread and availability of Internet broadband connections, mobile broadband communications, Web 2.0 and social networking. The most significant that has happened to the industry is the move of news consumption from print to online and the increasingly mobile nature of the news delivery channels. Additionally, the industry is also pressed by the increasing competition from the new untraditional types of international competitors - various portals, news aggregators and online classified advertisement sites. In this chapter, we look at how the major Danish newspapers are responding to the challenges posed by the decreasing sales of the printed newspapers and advertising space, growing online advertising and various technological innovations. We approach the theme from the business model perspective and discuss how the move to online and mobile news delivery channels forces the newspapers to revise and adjust their existing business models. Our data sources include industry reports, professional literature, academic research and a dozen of in-depth interviews with executives of the two leading Danish media holdings - JP / Politikens Hus and Berlingske Media.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Holm, Anna B.","Ulhøi, John Parm","Uliyanova, Anastasia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164061"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"krise og innovation i dagbladsindustriens forretningsmodeller","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.statsbiblioteket.dk/search/index.jsp?query=recordID:%22sb_5484478%22","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164061","ids":["au-3ce33a61-ebd3-407d-a346-e0fe2a64829f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C99888DE601C649E15F586C3A11BE559"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.statsbiblioteket.dk/search/index.jsp?query=recordID:%22sb_5484478%22","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management, Department of Business Administration - Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Borisovna","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"44f0d314-bb0b-4a13-b1aa-01dc8c5ff8b8","name":"Holm, Anna B.","name_org":"Holm, Anna Borisovna","orcid":"0000-0002-4060-4533","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John Parm","key":"ulhøipau","last":"Ulhøi","locid":"4d80510b-6b20-4e82-b6c7-70647d6449ac","name":"Ulhøi, John Parm","orcid":"0000-0002-2486-8010","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anastasia","key":"uliyanovapau","last":"Uliyanova","locid":"db01ee89-fd7c-4240-93d2-06d462912e3b","name":"Uliyanova, Anastasia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"brynskovpedh","last":"Brynskov","name":"Brynskov, Martin","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kim","key":"halskovpedh","last":"Halskov","name":"Halskov, Kim","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"kabelpedh","last":"Kabel","name":"Kabel, Lars","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788792816061"],"pages":"108-119","publisher":"Ajour","status":"p","title":"Byens Digitale Liv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3ce33a61-ebd3-407d-a346-e0fe2a64829f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Krise og innovation i dagbladsindustriens forretningsmodeller","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-164061","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
